<custom_item>
  type                     : REGISTRY_SETTING
  description              : "1.0072 - MSSRV - (L1) Ensure 'Configure Remote Encryption Protection Mode' is set to 'Enabled: Audit' or higher"
  info                     : "This policy setting configures the Brute-Force Protection feature in Microsoft Defender Antivirus."
  solution                 : "To establish the recommended configuration via GP, set the following UI path to Enabled: Audit or higher:

Computer Configuration\Policies\Administrative Templates\Windows Components\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\Remediation\Behavioral Network Blocks\Brute-Force Protection\Configure Remote Encryption Protection Mode

Note: This Group Policy path is provided by the Group Policy template WindowsDefender.admx/adml that is included with the Microsoft Windows 11 Release 24H2 Administrative Templates (or newer).

Impact:

Legitimate sign-ins and sessions could be detected or blocked by this feature if too many failed attempts are detected."
  reference                : "NIST 800-53r5|SI-3"
  see_also                 : "See HTH Policies and Standards"
  value_type               : POLICY_DWORD
  value_data               : "1" || "2"
  reg_key                  : "HKLM\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows Defender\Remediation\Behavioral Network Blocks\Brute Force Protection"
  reg_item                 : "BruteForceProtectionConfiguredState"
  reg_option               : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type                     : REGISTRY_SETTING
  description              : "1.0073 - MSSRV - (L1) Ensure 'Scan excluded files and directories during quick scans' is set to 'Enabled: 1'"
  info                     : "This policy setting manages whether or not Microsoft Defender Antivirus scans excluded files and directories when running a Quick Scan."
  solution                 : "To establish the recommended configuration via GP, set the following UI path to Enabled: 1 :

Computer Configuration\Policies\Administrative Templates\Windows Components\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\Scan\Scan excluded files and directories during quick scans

Note: This Group Policy path is provided by the Group Policy template WindowsDefender.admx/adml that is included with the Microsoft Windows 11 Release 24H2 Administrative Templates (or newer).

Impact:

A Quick Scan could take longer when including the contextually excluded files and directories."
  reference                : "NIST 800-53r5|SI-3"
  see_also                 : "See HTH Policies and Standards"
  value_type               : POLICY_DWORD
  value_data               : "1"
  reg_key                  : "HKLM\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows Defender\Scan"
  reg_item                 : "QuickScanIncludeExclusions"
  reg_option               : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
</custom_item>

